# The broker protocol's messages (docs/plugins.md 3.1, 3.4): the one source of sdk/plugmsg.h (the wire format in C,
# used by hassmic's broker and by the C client), of the message reference in sdk/PROTOCOL.md and of the test vectors,
# all made by tools/mkplugmsg.py and kept in git; `make unit-plugmsg` fails when they are not this file's, and when
# this file is not what sdk/scopes.lock recorded of every scope version (below).
#
#   scope NAME VERSION "what it is"            core (what every plugin speaks) and one per capability, named as it
#   version NAME N widens|within "what it adds" every version above 1: whether it lets a plugin do more than its
#                                               capability's line at install says (widens: an update that comes to
#                                               require it asks for the button), or only says more of the same
#   const NAME SCOPE[@N] VALUE
#   enum NAME SCOPE A=1 B=2@N>A C=3@N>- ...    values of a field; never renumbered.  A value of a version above 1
#                                               names (>) the value of an earlier version that a peer speaking an
#                                               earlier one gets in its place (pm_<enum>_for, pm_fit), or none (>-):
#                                               then the packet is not sent to such a peer at all, which only a
#                                               message marked drop may be (below).  CAP: one per capability, each its
#                                               scope's from that scope's version 1
#   keys CONTEXT SCOPE[@N] KEY ...              keys of the manifest where they stand (manifest, setting, net.lan ...)
#   msg NAME NUMBER DIR SCOPE[@N][|SCOPE[@N]] [drop] "what it is"
#                                               drop: it may go to a peer not at all, where a value it holds is one
#                                               that peer's version has no word for (>-); recorded with the message
#       TYPE name [MAX] [enum:E] [@N] "..."     u8 u16 u32 u64; str: u16 length + bytes, MAX bytes at most, no NUL;
#                                               bytes: the same, any byte (a value the plugin keeps).  enum:E: a
#                                               number that holds E_*'s values, one the peer speaks (else malformed)
#       list name MAX [@N] "what it is"         MAX elements at most; one level of lists inside.  On the wire: a u16
#           TYPE name ...                       count where the field stands, the elements after the last field of the
#                                               struct the list is in (of several lists: in their order)
#   DIR: > plugin to broker, < broker to plugin, = either.  SCOPE: the scope the message is part of, which is the
#   capability a plugin needs for it (core: none); a|b: part of either (a plugin with either capability may use it;
#   its enums are core's or CAP only: a peer of one of its scopes may not speak another's).
#   @N: the scope's version that brought it (1 where none is written).
#
# Versions (sdk/PROTOCOL.md "Versions"): a plugin's manifest names the least version of each scope it speaks
# ("requires"), and hassmic speaks exactly that with it.  A scope's next version only adds: a message, a field
# appended after every field of an earlier version (at every level of the message), an enum value, a constant, a
# key of the manifest.
# Nothing changes meaning, type, bound, number or direction, and nothing goes: what must break is a new scope.
# A value's fallback is the value a peer of the earlier version should act on, as that peer understands it: the one
# the new value is a case of (a call that ended "elsewhere" ended: STOPPED; a failure of a new kind: FAILED).  Never a
# failure or refusal mapped to a success, never a command mapped to another command, never an event to one that did
# not happen (a new key of the buttons is not the action button to a plugin that knows only that one).  `>-` (no
# earlier value is right: the packet goes to a peer of that version not at all, its sender drops it without a word
# as what that peer cannot be told, and the reference says so) only where the enum is what the message is about: an
# event whose whole point is the new value, on a message marked drop (BUTTON: a key a button-1 plugin does not
# have).  Never on an answer (ERR), an end (CALL_END, CALL_HANGUP, REQ_END), a state (STATE, MUSIC_STATE) or a reason
# or qualifier of something else (MWHY, FROM, REQSRC, WAKE_FAIL, FILE_BAD): what those say must arrive, so a new
# value there names the earlier one it is a case of, and one that is a case of none, a new command among them, is a
# new message.  tools/mkplugmsg.py refuses `>-` on an enum that a message not marked drop holds, the greeting, OK and
# ERR are never marked, and the lock records the mark.  The fallback is recorded with the value: it never changes.  A message of several scopes, and the greeting (HELLO, WELCOME, REFUSED), never grow: their lists of
# scopes hold 255, every scope there will ever be.  tools/mkplugmsg.py refuses what breaks these rules, and
# sdk/scopes.lock holds what each recorded version had: a recorded version that messages.def no longer makes fails the
# build, and so does one that any release (a tag v*, of main or of release) carried and that is here otherwise, a line
# taken out or added.
#
# A packet: u16 type, u16 flags (0), u32 id, then the fields in order, little-endian, 32 kB at most, and nothing
# after them.  id ties an answer to its request (the asker picks it, never 0); events have 0, but for LOG, which the
# plugin answers (flow control).  Numbers are the wire's: never reused.

scope core 1 "what every plugin speaks: the greeting, its settings, READY, PING, STOP, the time, OK and ERR"
scope storage 1 "data of its own on the Echo"
scope files 1 "the files the owner uploads on its card"
scope state 1 "what the Echo does: idle, listening, thinking, speaking; mute; volume"
scope log.read 1 "hassmic's log without what was said, names and addresses"
scope log.read.full 1 "the log as the settings page shows it (official plugins only)"
scope net.server 1 "sockets to the server the owner enters"
scope net.lan 1 "sockets to addresses on the local network"
scope net.internet 1 "sockets to the internet"
scope net.udp 1 "UDP ports of its own"
scope net.discover 1 "a search of the network"
scope audio.music 1 "a music source"
scope audio.volume 1 "the Echo's volume"
scope call 1 "calls: a ring, the room's audio while one is live"
scope wake 1 "the microphone stream all the time; wake words"
scope request.audio 1 "a copy of each request's audio"
scope request.text 1 "each request's transcript and reply"
scope ha.entities 1 "entities in Home Assistant"
scope ha.actions 1 "actions Home Assistant calls"
scope button 1 "presses and holds of the Echo's buttons"

const MAX_PACKET core 32768

enum ERR        core UNKNOWN=1 DENIED=2 BAD=3 BUSY=4 LIMIT=5 NOT_FOUND=6 FAILED=7 UNSET=8
enum MUSIC      audio.music PLAYING=1 PAUSED=2 STOPPED=3
enum MCMD       audio.music PAUSE=1 RESUME=2 STOP=3 NEXT=4 PREVIOUS=5
enum MWHY       audio.music BUTTON=1 STOP_WORD=2 OTHER_SOURCE=3 HOME_ASSISTANT=4
enum STATE      state IDLE=0 LISTENING=1 THINKING=2 SPEAKING=3
enum FROM       ha.actions HOME_ASSISTANT=1 PAGE=2
enum HANGUP     call BUTTON=1 SPOKEN=2 SCREEN=3 NOT_ANSWERED=4 NOT_LIVE=5 STOPPED=6
enum RESULT     call HUNG_UP=1 BUSY=2 DECLINED=3 NO_ANSWER=4 FAILED=5
enum REFUSED    core SCOPES=1 STATE=2
enum REQSRC     request.audio WAKE_WORD=1 BUTTON=2 FOLLOW_UP=3 HA_WAKE=4
enum REQEND     request.audio HA=1 HEARD_HERE=2 CANCELLED=3 TIMEOUT=4 ERROR=5 LINK_LOST=6 MUTED=7
enum REQTEXT    request.text HEARD=1 REPLY=2
enum WAKE_FAIL  wake NO_MODEL=1 BAD_MODEL=2 MEMORY=3 UNSUPPORTED=4 OTHER=5
enum FILE_BAD   files FORMAT=1 UNSUPPORTED=2 TOO_LARGE=3 MISSING=4 OTHER=5
enum BUTTON_KEY button ACTION=1 VOLUME_UP=2 VOLUME_DOWN=3
enum BUTTON_HOW button PRESS=1 HOLD=2
# a capability's number: CONNECT's and UDP_OPEN's kind (WELCOME says what was granted as the scopes spoken)
enum CAP        core STORAGE=0 FILES=1 STATE=2 LOG_READ=3 LOG_READ_FULL=4 NET_SERVER=5 NET_LAN=6 NET_INTERNET=7 NET_UDP=8 NET_DISCOVER=9 AUDIO_MUSIC=10 AUDIO_VOLUME=11 CALL=12 WAKE=13 REQUEST_AUDIO=14 REQUEST_TEXT=15 HA_ENTITIES=16 HA_ACTIONS=17 BUTTON=18

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the manifest's keys (sdk/PROTOCOL.md "The manifest")
# Where each stands (a context: the manifest itself, a setting, a capability's entry) and the scope version that
# brought it.  A manifest that uses a key of a later version than it requires of that scope is refused, by the Echo
# and by the plugin index alike (plugin_store.c ps_manifest_parse, hassmic-plugins' tools/index.py manifest_check);
# a key no build knows is refused where the context is strict (a capability's entries) and left alone where it is
# not (the manifest itself, a setting: a key the Echo reads nothing of)
keys manifest           core id name author version version_name source license description requires author_key digest memory_mb threads models capabilities settings
keys setting            core name label type help unit min max options default item max_items fields catalog
keys setting.item       files by files
keys setting.item.file  files suffix as max_kb optional
keys setting.field      files name label type min max step
keys net.server         net.server setting proto ports
keys net.discover       net.discover udp to
keys net.lan            net.lan proto ports
keys net.internet       net.internet proto ports
keys ha.entities.binary_sensor ha.entities name kind label icon page
keys ha.entities.sensor        ha.entities name kind label icon page unit decimals
keys ha.entities.text_sensor   ha.entities name kind label icon page
keys ha.entities.switch        ha.entities name kind label icon page
keys ha.entities.button        ha.entities name kind label icon page
keys ha.entities.number        ha.entities name kind label icon page unit min max step
keys ha.entities.select        ha.entities name kind label icon page options
keys ha.entities.event         ha.entities name kind label icon page types
keys ha.actions         ha.actions name label args page calls
keys ha.actions.arg     ha.actions name type

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- core
msg HELLO 1 > core "The first message, and the plugin's: every scope its client speaks, each at the highest version it has (its sdk/messages.def's).  The greeting never grows."
    u32 sdk "the client library's version, for the log"
    list scopes 255 "the scopes, each once"
        str name 24 ""
        u16 version "1 or more"
msg WELCOME 2 < core "The answer to HELLO: where it runs, and the version of each scope spoken with it from here on: exactly its manifest's requires (hassmic sends it nothing of a later version, and takes nothing of one), which is also what it was granted (core and the scope of each capability the owner accepted).  The greeting never grows."
    u32 clock_set "1: the wall clock is set (it comes from Home Assistant)"
    str model 48 "the Echo's model, as Home Assistant shows it"
    str node 64 "its node name"
    str name 64 "its name"
    str zone 64 "the time zone: a name or a POSIX rule, empty while unknown"
    list scopes 255 "the scopes spoken, each once: core and those of its capabilities (what the owner accepted)"
        str name 24 ""
        u16 version ""
msg REFUSED 3 < core "The answer to a HELLO hassmic cannot serve; the plugin ends.  SCOPES: its client does not speak a scope at the version its manifest requires (HELLO named it lower, or not at all); STATE: a HELLO out of turn.  The greeting never grows."
    u16 why enum:REFUSED "REFUSED_*"
msg CONFIG 4 < core "The plugin's settings, all of them: after WELCOME and whenever the owner changes one."
    list settings 32 ""
        str name 32 ""
        str value 512 "as text: a bool is 0 or 1"
msg READY 5 > core "The plugin has its settings and runs.  Until then hassmic sends it nothing but CONFIG and FILES."
msg PING 6 < core "Every 10 s; three unanswered and the plugin is killed."
msg PONG 7 > core "The answer, with PING's id."
msg STOP 8 < core "End now: 2 s, then SIGTERM."
msg TIME 9 < core "The clock was set, or the time zone changed."
    u32 clock_set ""
    str zone 64 ""
msg OK 10 = core "A request went through (the request's id).  A descriptor the request asked for comes with it.  From the plugin: a LOG handled (the LOG's id)."
msg ERR 11 = core "A request did not (the request's id)."
    u16 code enum:ERR "ERR_*"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- files (the owner uploads, the plugin reads)
msg FILES 20 < files "One list of uploaded items: after CONFIG and whenever the owner adds, edits or deletes one."
    str list 32 "the files setting's name"
    list items 64 ""
        str id 40 ""
        u8 checked "1: the plugin said FILE_OK to it"
        str title 64 "what FILE_OK named it"
        list fields 16 "the owner's values of the item's fields"
            str name 32 ""
            str value 256 ""
        list files 8 ""
            str name 64 "the file's suffix, as the manifest names it"
            u32 size ""
msg FILE_OPEN 21 > files "One file of an item: OK comes with a read-only descriptor of it."
    str list 32 ""
    str item 40 ""
    str file 64 "its suffix"
msg FILE_CHECK 22 < files "The owner uploaded this item: can the plugin use it?  5 s for FILE_OK or FILE_BAD (this id)."
    str list 32 ""
    str item 40 ""
msg FILE_OK 23 > files "The item is good."
    str title 64 "for its row on the page (a wake word model: the phrase)"
    list fields 16 "start values of its fields, read out of the file"
        str name 32 ""
        str value 256 ""
msg FILE_BAD 24 > files "The item cannot be used; it is not kept."
    u16 code enum:FILE_BAD "FILE_BAD_*"
    str why 200 "shown as text"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- wake (the microphone stream, all the time)
# The stream comes with the first WAKE_OPEN: SOCK_SEQPACKET, each packet a u64 position (samples since hassmic's
# start), then one block of 16 kHz mono s16le, WAKE_SAMPLES_MAX samples at most (hassmic cuts a longer capture block
# into several, each with its own position; a reader's buffer of 8 + 2 * WAKE_SAMPLES_MAX bytes takes every packet
# whole: a SOCK_SEQPACKET read into less cuts the packet and loses its rest, a review of 6631974, 9)
const WAKE_SAMPLES_MAX wake 4096
msg WAKE_WORDS 30 > wake "The items the plugin can listen for: at start and whenever they change.  Ids only: the phrases are hassmic's, fixed when the owner uploaded each item."
    str list 32 "the files setting they are items of"
    list words 16 ""
        str id 40 ""
msg WAKE_OPEN 31 < wake "Listen for this word in this slot.  The first one comes with the stream's descriptor.  5 s for WAKE_READY or WAKE_FAILED."
    u8 slot "0 or 1"
    str word 40 ""
msg WAKE_READY 32 > wake "The slot's word is loaded and listening."
    u8 slot ""
msg WAKE_FAILED 33 > wake "The slot's word could not be loaded."
    u8 slot ""
    u16 why enum:WAKE_FAIL "WAKE_FAIL_*"
msg WAKE_CLOSE 34 < wake "Stop listening in this slot."
    u8 slot ""
msg WAKE_RESET 35 < wake "The audio has a gap (hassmic played something, the capture restarted): forget what was heard."
msg WAKE_HEARD 36 > wake "The slot's word, between two positions of the stream.  Checked by hassmic: begin < end, end not ahead of the stream and at most 300 ms behind it, 0.3 to 1.5 s long, one a second."
    u8 slot ""
    u8 score "how sure, 0..255"
    u64 begin "samples, on the stream's clock"
    u64 end ""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- storage (the plugin writes)
msg STORE_GET 40 > storage "The value kept under a key: answered STORE_VALUE (this id), or ERR NOT_FOUND."
    str key 48 "[a-z0-9._-], 1 to 48, not beginning with a dot, not ending in .tmp and digits"
msg STORE_VALUE 41 < storage "The answer to STORE_GET."
    bytes value 16384 ""
msg STORE_PUT 42 > storage "Keep this value under this key, in place of what was there.  OK; ERR LIMIT: over the accepted kB (or 128 keys); ERR BUSY: written too often (10 writes, then one a minute: the Echo's flash), try again later."
    str key 48 ""
    bytes value 16384 ""
msg STORE_DEL 43 > storage "The key and its value away (a write as STORE_PUT is).  OK, or ERR NOT_FOUND."
    str key 48 ""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the log (log.read, log.read.full)
msg LOG_FOLLOW 50 > log.read|log.read.full "Send the log from here on (LOG events) until the plugin ends.  OK, or ERR BAD for a cursor that is none.  Asked again: from there instead."
    str from 40 "a cursor of a LOG before (after a restart: what was written meanwhile); start: the oldest line kept; empty: from now"
msg LOG 51 < log.read|log.read.full "Lines of hassmic's log, whole and in order: under log.read without what was said, names and addresses; under log.read.full (official plugins only) as the settings page shows them, what was said included, but for a wake word plugin's lines and the Sendspin pairing token (sdk/PROTOCOL.md).  It has an id: the plugin must answer OK (that id) once it has handled the lines, and the next LOG comes only after that OK (flow control; unanswered for 10 s, hassmic says so).  A plugin that falls behind loses nothing that is still kept."
    str cursor 40 "where the next LOG begins: keep it to go on from there"
    u8 gap "1: lines between the cursor asked for and these are gone (the log was rotated twice meanwhile)"
    list lines 64 ""
        str line 1024 "one line, with its time in front; no line end"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the network (net.server, net.lan, net.internet)
msg CONNECT 60 > net.server|net.lan|net.internet "A socket by one of the capability's entries: OK comes with it, connected and non-blocking (TCP), or connected (UDP: send() reaches that address only).  The plugin's to keep and close; hassmic keeps no copy.  net.server: the server the owner entered; net.lan: an address on the local network the plugin names (private or link-local, a.b.c.d, never a name), never at DNS's ports 53 and 853; net.internet: an address or name on the internet the plugin names, never one on the local network (also not what a name resolves to).  Never loopback, the Echo's own addresses, multicast, broadcast, 0.0.0.0/8 or port 5555.  ERR DENIED: not that entry's host or port, not the kind's address, not the plugin's capability; UNSET: the owner has not entered the server; NOT_FOUND: its name has no address; FAILED: no connection (10 s for all of it); BUSY: two under way, or 30 in the last minute, or its name's lookup not begun (two of the plugin's own still under way, or the Echo's at its bound); BAD: before READY, no host for net.lan or net.internet, a host that is no name or address, port 0 where the entry has more than one."
    u8 kind enum:CAP "the capability (CAP_NET_SERVER, CAP_NET_LAN, CAP_NET_INTERNET)"
    u8 entry "the entry's place in that capability's list, from 0"
    str host 253 "net.server: empty, the server the owner entered (anything else must be that, as written).  net.lan: an IPv4 address, a.b.c.d.  net.internet: a host name or an IPv4 address"
    u16 port "0: the entry's (its only port, or for net.server the one in its port setting); else one the entry allows (any but 5555 for \"any\", for net.lan also but 53 and 853)"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- UDP of its own, discovery, proposals (net.udp, net.discover, net.server)
msg UDP_OPEN 61 > net.udp|net.discover "A UDP socket bound to a port of the plugin's own (28940 to 28999, the same at every start): answered UDP_OPENED (this id) with its descriptor.  It hears only private and link-local senders.  kind CAP_NET_UDP: one of the manifest's net.udp count (entry from 0); CAP_NET_DISCOVER: the socket that searches (entry 0), BROADCAST's.  ERR DENIED: not the plugin's capability or entry; BUSY: that one is open; LIMIT: no port left; BAD: before READY."
    u8 kind enum:CAP "CAP_NET_UDP or CAP_NET_DISCOVER"
    u8 entry ""
msg UDP_OPENED 62 < net.udp|net.discover "The answer to UDP_OPEN, with the socket (receive with recv or recvfrom; send with send once UDP_PEER fixed its peer, or by SENDTO)."
    u8 handle "what UDP_PEER, SENDTO and BROADCAST name it by"
    u16 port "the port it is bound to"
msg UDP_PEER 63 > net.udp "Fix the peer of a net.udp socket: send() reaches that address and port only, and only it is heard.  A private or link-local unicast address the Echo routes out of its network interface, never the Echo's own, loopback, port 5555 or DNS's 53 and 853.  A new peer once a second, two at once.  OK; ERR DENIED (the address), BAD (no such handle), BUSY (over the rate)."
    u8 handle ""
    u32 address "IPv4: a.b.c.d as (a << 24) | (b << 16) | (c << 8) | d"
    u16 port ""
msg SENDTO 64 > net.udp "One datagram from a net.udp socket to an address as UDP_PEER allows them; sent without waiting (dropped when the socket's queue is full).  50 a second.  An answer only to an id that is not 0: OK, or ERR DENIED, BAD, BUSY (over the rate)."
    u8 handle ""
    u32 address ""
    u16 port ""
    bytes data 1472 ""
msg BROADCAST 65 > net.discover "The search: one datagram from the net.discover socket to the manifest's port, on every network the Echo is on (each one's broadcast address) or to the manifest's multicast group.  Once a second.  Answers come to that socket.  An answer only to an id that is not 0: OK, or ERR BAD, BUSY."
    u8 handle ""
    bytes data 1472 ""
msg PROPOSE 66 > net.server "What the plugin found, offered to the owner for a host row its net.server names: shown on its card ('Found 192.168.1.20. Use it?'), written only by the owner's click.  A private or link-local IPv4 address as text; one per row at a time, a minute apart.  OK; ERR DENIED (not such a row, not such an address), BUSY (within the minute), BAD."
    str setting 32 ""
    str value 15 "a.b.c.d"
msg NET 67 < net.server|net.lan|net.internet|net.udp|net.discover "The Echo's address on its network, to a plugin with a net capability: after READY and whenever it changes."
    u32 address "as UDP_PEER's; 0 while it has none"
    u32 mask ""
    u8 up "1: on a network"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- music (audio.music, audio.volume)
msg MUSIC_OPEN 70 > audio.music "Play: OK comes with a stream socket (SOCK_STREAM, non-blocking) into which the plugin writes s16le at this rate and these channels; what it writes plays on the Echo's speaker as music (ducked under the voice assistant, at the music's volume).  The newest music source wins: Sendspin and a phone over Bluetooth are paused.  Rates 8000, 11025, 16000, 22050, 24000, 32000, 44100, 48000; 1 or 2 channels.  ERR BAD: a format it does not take, BUSY: open already (MUSIC_CLOSE first), LIMIT: ten in a minute."
    u32 rate ""
    u8 channels ""
msg MUSIC_STATE 71 > audio.music "What the plugin's player does now: the button, the stop word and Home Assistant's media player go by it.  PLAYING with a stream open makes it the newest source; title and artist go to its card.  An answer only to an id that is not 0."
    u8 state enum:MUSIC "MUSIC_*"
    str title 128 ""
    str artist 128 ""
msg MUSIC_CLOSE 72 > audio.music "The stream ends: what was written plays out, then the output closes.  OK."
msg MUSIC_POS 73 < audio.music "Where the stream is, five times a second while it is open: what a player needs to say where it is (and to keep a group in step)."
    u64 frames "frames that reached the speaker"
    u64 at "when, on the monotonic clock (CLOCK_MONOTONIC, microseconds)"
    u32 queued "microseconds written and not played yet"
msg MUSIC_CMD 74 < audio.music "Do this to what plays: from the action button, the stop word, another source that started or a Drop In call (OTHER_SOURCE), Home Assistant's media player."
    u8 cmd enum:MCMD "MCMD_*"
    u8 why enum:MWHY "MWHY_*"
msg VOLUME_SET 75 > audio.volume "Set the Echo's volume (as the keys do; a burst sets it at once and then to its last value, 500 ms apart at most; the last value is dropped if the volume is set elsewhere before it, and VOLUME says what it is): OK; ERR BUSY over five a second or twenty a minute."
    u8 percent "0..100"
msg VOLUME 76 < audio.volume "The Echo's volume moved, from wherever: after READY and on every change."
    u8 percent ""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the assistant's state (state)
msg STATE 80 < state "What the Echo does: after READY and on every change of any of it.  Never what was said."
    u8 state enum:STATE "STATE_*"
    u8 muted "1: the microphones are off (the button's latch or Home Assistant's switch)"
    u8 volume "0..100"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Home Assistant's entities and actions (ha.entities, ha.actions)
msg ENTITY_STATE 90 > ha.entities "An entity's state, as text: a sensor's number, a binary sensor's or switch's on/off, a number within its limits, a select's option, a text sensor's text (255 bytes).  Ten a second for all of the plugin's.  An answer only to an id that is not 0: OK, or ERR BAD (no such entity, a value it cannot take), BUSY."
    str name 32 "the manifest's"
    str value 255 ""
msg EVENT 91 > ha.entities "An event entity fires one of its types.  Counted with ENTITY_STATE."
    str name 32 ""
    str type 32 ""
msg ENTITY_SET 92 < ha.entities "Home Assistant set a switch, number or select of the plugin's, or pressed its button (value empty).  The plugin answers with ENTITY_STATE once it is so."
    str name 32 ""
    str value 255 ""
msg ACTION 93 < ha.actions "One of the plugin's actions, called by Home Assistant (its keyed link) or by the owner's button on its card."
    str name 32 ""
    u8 from enum:FROM "FROM_*"
    str token 32 "call: a call token (32 hex digits) when the manifest marks the action \"calls\" (both of its ways in are a person's: Home Assistant's keyed link, an approved browser); else empty.  One use, for CALL_OUT only (a call going out), within 10 s; it answers no call coming in"
    list args 4 "in the manifest's order"
        str name 32 ""
        str value 255 "an int as its digits"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- calls (call)
msg CALL_INCOMING 100 > call "A call comes in: the Echo rings (its ringtone, its light, on a Show the plugin's name beside WHO) until a person answers here (CALL_ANSWER) or it ends.  OK: it rings; ERR BUSY: another call is on (a Drop In, another plugin's, this one's), or a ring asked faster than its looks at the line allow: each ring refused busy costs one, one a second come back and two at most kept, and with none left it is refused busy without a look; DENIED: do not disturb, or the microphones are off; LIMIT: three rings of this plugin unanswered in the last ten minutes; BAD: before READY."
    str who 64 "the caller as the plugin names it (a number, a name): shown, never interpreted"
msg CALL_ANSWER 101 < call "A person here answered the ringing call (the action button, the Show's screen): answer it on the far side, then CALL_LIVE."
msg CALL_HANGUP 102 < call "hassmic ended the call (any state): end it on the far side.  No CALL_END is needed after it."
    u8 why enum:HANGUP "HANGUP_*"
msg CALL_OUT 103 > call "Place a call: only with a token an ACTION marked calls just brought (a person asked for it).  The Echo shows the call going out.  OK; ERR DENIED: no such token, used, older than 10 s, or the microphones are off; BUSY: another call is on; BAD."
    str token 32 ""
    str who 64 "whom it calls, as shown"
msg CALL_RINGING_THERE 104 > call "The far side rings (a call going out).  For the log.  An answer only to an id that is not 0."
msg CALL_LIVE 105 > call "The call is connected on the far side: OK comes with the call's audio socket (SOCK_SEQPACKET; each packet a u32 sequence number, then 20 ms of 16 kHz mono s16le, 644 bytes: the room's microphone from hassmic, the far side's voice to hassmic).  An incoming call only once a person answered it here, at the Echo (CALL_ANSWER); no token answers one.  ERR DENIED: not answered here; BAD: no call of this plugin's in that state."
    str token 32 "not looked at (a token is for CALL_OUT only): send it empty.  Kept: a field of call 1's layout; read as every text field is, so one that is not a string (a NUL inside, longer than 32 bytes) is BAD"
msg CALL_END 106 > call "The call ended on the far side, or the plugin ends it: in any state.  OK."
    u8 result enum:RESULT "RESULT_*"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- a request's copy (request.audio, request.text)
# The audio comes on a socket of its own per request, handed over with REQ_START: SOCK_SEQPACKET, each packet a u32
# run number and a u32 offset (samples since the run's first, the lead-in's zeros included; a gap: blocks dropped),
# then one block exactly as Home Assistant got it, 16 kHz mono s16le, REQ_SAMPLES_MAX samples at most.  hassmic's end
# is closed after the run's last block: read it to its end
const REQ_SAMPLES_MAX request.audio 2048
msg REQ_START 110 < request.audio "A request begins: a copy of what Home Assistant is sent comes on the socket that comes with this message, until REQ_END.  Only the Echo that streams the request has one; with the wake word in Home Assistant (-w remote) from its wake word on.  Nothing can be sent back: the plugin hears, it never takes part."
    u32 run "the request's number, new with each (the audio's packets carry it)"
    u8 source enum:REQSRC "REQSRC_*: the wake word heard here, the action button, a follow-up Home Assistant asked for, the wake word heard in Home Assistant"
    u8 slot "the wake word's slot (0 or 1) for REQSRC_WAKE_WORD, else 0"
    str phrase 64 "the wake word's phrase that goes to Home Assistant with the request"
msg REQ_END 111 < request.audio "The request's audio ended (the microphone off): the socket has its last block and then its end."
    u32 run ""
    u8 why enum:REQEND "REQEND_*: Home Assistant ended it (it heard enough, or ended its run), the end heard here, cancelled (the button, stop, a new wake word), the pipeline's timeout, an error, the link lost, the microphones muted (the button's latch or Home Assistant's switch)"
    u32 samples "samples the copy had (what Home Assistant got of it)"
    u32 dropped "of them not sent to the plugin: its socket was full (it did not read in time)"
msg REQ_TEXT 112 < request.text "What speech to text understood of a request, or the assistant's answer, as Home Assistant reports them (Wyoming: the transcript only).  A bare stop or wake word that the Echo acts on itself is not passed on."
    u32 run "the request's number, as REQ_START's (a plugin without request.audio gets only this)"
    u8 kind enum:REQTEXT "REQTEXT_*"
    str text 1024 ""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the buttons (button)
msg BUTTON 120 < button drop "A button of the Echo was pressed or held a second: exactly what Home Assistant's \"Button\" event entity hears (the same moment, the same exclusions): never a press that served a wait for the button (a login of the settings page, adb, a plugin's install, a withdrawn plugin run anyway, a phone's setup over Bluetooth), never a hold that served the settings page's note, never a skip of a double or triple press.  The plugin only hears: what the button does on the Echo happens all the same, and nothing it answers changes that.  Five a second, ten at once: more are dropped, and the log counts them."
    u8 key enum:BUTTON_KEY "BUTTON_KEY_*: the action button, volume up, volume down"
    u8 how enum:BUTTON_HOW "BUTTON_HOW_*: pressed (let go within a second), held a second (still down)"
